# HSM collector conformance v1 — double wire-text matrix.
# Pins the EXACT canonical text of double payload values across languages:
# the .NET Core 3.0+ shortest round-trip form — what double.ToString("R") and
# System.Text.Json print on .NET 8: shortest digits that parse back to the same
# double, fixed notation for decimal exponents in [-4, 16] (every value below
# 1e17 down to 0.0001), otherwise scientific with uppercase 'E', signed
# exponent, at least two exponent digits (1E+17, 1E-05). The native serializer
# produces it with std::to_chars digits + those layout rules; the managed driver
# runs on net48, whose own "R" differs (17-digit fallback, scientific from
# 1e15), so it computes the same text itself (CanonicalDoubleText, #1528).
# This is the #1 silent killer for wire parity: tolerant numeric assertions
# (expect_bar_field) cannot catch formatting drift, so these cases assert the
# serialized text itself. Trailing comma in every substring anchors the end of
# the value token (so 0.1 cannot match 0.1000...).
#
# Deliberately excluded:
# - negative zero: .NET Core prints "-0"; net48 "R" and the native formatter
#   print "0", and so does the managed driver.
# - NaN / ±Infinity never serialize: the collector rejects them at the API
#   boundary (pinned in instant_mixed_contract / bar_double_contract).

double_wire_text_matrix|create_collector
double_wire_text_matrix|create_double_sensor|contract/number-format/matrix
double_wire_text_matrix|start
